<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:144%;">Appendix for LiLo-VLA</span></p>
</div>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Overview</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This supplementary material provides comprehensive details supporting the main paper.
Section <a href="#S7" title="VII Additional Experimental Results ‣ LiLo-VLA: Compositional Long-Horizon Manipulation via Linked Object-Centric Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VII</span></a> presents qualitative visualizations of our real-world experiments, highlighting specific mechanisms for robustness and failure recovery.
Section <a href="#S8" title="VIII Benchmark Details ‣ LiLo-VLA: Compositional Long-Horizon Manipulation via Linked Object-Centric Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VIII</span></a> defines the full atomic skill library and details the exact task sequences for the LIBERO-Long++ and Ultra-Long benchmarks.
Section <a href="#S9" title="IX Extended Methodology Details ‣ LiLo-VLA: Compositional Long-Horizon Manipulation via Linked Object-Centric Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IX</span></a> elaborates on the relative pose representation designed to ensure zero-shot generalization to novel workspace configurations.
Section <a href="#S10" title="X Data Efficiency and Combinatorial Complexity ‣ LiLo-VLA: Compositional Long-Horizon Manipulation via Linked Object-Centric Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">X</span></a> offers a theoretical analysis of the combinatorial complexity involved in long-horizon tasks, demonstrating the data efficiency of our modular approach.
Section <a href="#S11" title="XI Training and Implementation Details ‣ LiLo-VLA: Compositional Long-Horizon Manipulation via Linked Object-Centric Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XI</span></a> outlines the training objectives, hyperparameters, and the success checker heuristics utilized in our implementation.
Finally, Section <a href="#S12" title="XII Hardware and System Setup ‣ LiLo-VLA: Compositional Long-Horizon Manipulation via Linked Object-Centric Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XII</span></a> describes the hardware specifications and perception models utilized in our real-world system.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VII </span><span id="S7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Additional Experimental Results</span></h2>

<figure id="S7.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.21531v1/images/real_all.png" id="S7.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/378;" width="476" height="378" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. S1: </span><span id="S7.F1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qualitative Real-World Experimental Results.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S7.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">VII-A</span> </span><span id="S7.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Real-World Task Specifications</span></h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To evaluate the compositional generalization of LiLo-VLA, we define a library of 8 unique atomic skills across three distinct scenes. Table <a href="#S7.T1" title="TABLE S1 ‣ VII-A Real-World Task Specifications ‣ VII Additional Experimental Results ‣ LiLo-VLA: Compositional Long-Horizon Manipulation via Linked Object-Centric Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S1</span></a> defines these primitives, while Table <a href="#S7.T2" title="TABLE S2 ‣ VII-A Real-World Task Specifications ‣ VII Additional Experimental Results ‣ LiLo-VLA: Compositional Long-Horizon Manipulation via Linked Object-Centric Policies" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S2</span></a> details the exact execution sequences for all 8 evaluation tasks.</p>
</div>
